  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Your roof likely needs replacement if it is over 20 years old, shows curling or missing shingles, or leaks during heavy Utah snowmelt and storms.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "over 20 years old, shows curling or missing shingles, or leaks during heavy Utah snowmelt and storms"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Signs of Roof Failure"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Age of the Roof: Most standard asphalt shingle roofs in Utah last between 15 and 30 years. If your roof is past this mark, materials break down from intense UV rays and freeze-thaw cycles.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Damaged or Missing Shingles: Look for cracked, warped, curling, or entirely missing shingles. Granules piling up in your gutters also mean the protective surface of the shingle is gone.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ice Dams and Leaks: Utah\u2019s heavy winter snow can cause ice dams, leading to water stains on your ceilings, damp attic insulation, or mold growth.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sagging Roof Deck: A drooping or spongy roofline indicates structural moisture damage and rotting wooden decking underneath."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Damaged Flashing: Rust, cracks, or loose metal flashing around your chimney, vents, and skylights let water seep directly into your home."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Utah-Specific Factors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Severe Weather: Heavy winter snow loads, ice damming, and high seasonal winds strain roofing structures across the Wasatch Back and statewide."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Replacement Cost: Replacing a standard asphalt shingle roof in Utah typically costs between $8,000 and $25,000 depending on your home's size and roof pitch."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want, tell me:"
